 ## Stress analysis (FEA)
-- `backend/src/cad_assist/fem/`: `element.py` (C3D10, Gmsh node order, 4-point Gauss, stresses extrapolated and averaged; 6-node triangle tractions), `mesh.py` (Gmsh in a spawned child process: its high-order optimiser can abort the process; curved, then optimised, then straight-sided, inverted-element check), `solve.py` (AMG-CG, rigid-body near-nullspace), `analysis.py` (reactions from in-plane statics, cosine bearing with exact resultants, 3-2-1 hold whose reactions must be ~0, regions, margins), `job.py` (background job, results saved to `<project>/fem/`), `sizing.py` (recipe-level sizing for a target margin).
+- `backend/src/cad_assist/fem/`: `element.py` (C3D10, Gmsh node order, 4-point Gauss, stresses extrapolated and averaged; 6-node triangle tractions), `mesh.py` (Gmsh in a spawned child process: its high-order optimiser can abort the process; curved, then optimised, then straight-sided, inverted-element check), `solve.py` (AMG-CG, rigid-body near-nullspace), `analysis.py` (reactions from in-plane statics, cosine bearing with exact resultants; pins held square by forks (`Bore.tilt`, auto = forked end) react the out-of-plane couple through a stiff spring on each bore's least-squares tilt, applied as a low-rank term with a Woodbury-updated AMG preconditioner; the hold then keeps 4 DOFs and its reactions must be ~0; regions, margins), `job.py` (background job, results saved to `<project>/fem/`), `sizing.py` (recipe-level sizing for a target margin).
 - Mesh controls (`fem/controls.py`, project `mesh`): global size / curvature, edge divisions, mapped faces, spheres of influence. Edges and faces are kept by centre of mass and size (re-found on a rebuilt part and inside Gmsh), not by index. `propose()` is the best-practice rules; `ai/mesh_plan.py` has Claude propose controls, meshing and measuring each (elements around / through each bore, scaled-Jacobian quality, DOF and memory). A checked mesh is reused by the solve when its key (controls + part) matches. The convergence check re-solves with every size x1.5.
 - The solver reports progress (stage, CG residual per iteration against rtol) through `monitor` into `FemJob.progress` for the solve-status window. `FemRunner.job` is the latest job of any kind; `results_job` the latest analysis or sizing.
 - Every new analysis capability gets a closed-form benchmark in `tests/test_fem.py` before it is trusted. Peaks are taken over every node (mid-edge nodes included) so they bound the contour.
